# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QLNN_ukstep26_2 — TGLF settings of the training database (STEP / ukstep26,
# runTGLFdb production_run_2, sat1_em_azf-1, OLCF Defiant, Aug 2026).
#
# The switches in the "UK STEP recommended settings" block are the ones the
# UKAEA STEP team recommends for TGLF on STEP, based on their comparisons with
# nonlinear gyrokinetic (CGYRO/GENE) runs. They were forced onto every case by
# runTGLFdb (src/runTGLFdb.jl `run_tglf`, device == "ukstep26") on top of the
# ig2it-generated input.tglf. A QLNN prediction is only meaningful with these
# settings: the QL weights were computed with NBASIS_MAX=10 / WIDTH=1.9 /
# THETA_TRAPPED(r/R), and run_qlnn feeds them through TJLF's SAT_RULE=1 rule
# with the ALPHA_ZF / UNITS of the input.
#
# Species layout: the DATABASE ran TGLF with NS=4 unbundled species
# (1 = e, 2 = D, 3 = T, 4 = one lumped impurity; cases with thermal He ash
# had it folded into the impurity by lump_he_ukstep26!, charge and Zeff
# conserving). The NEURAL NETS were trained on the (e, DT, imp) lumping of
# those inputs (TrainQLweightNN species layout :ukstep26_dt). run_qlnn lumps
# an NS=4/5 input automatically via `qlnn_lump_dt` (AS_2+AS_3; TAUS/RLTS/
# RLNS/VPAR density-weighted; MASS_2 = density-weighted D/T mass in m_D units,
# 1.00 for pure D .. 1.25 for 50/50 D-T; impurity slot 4 -> 3). An NS=3
# (e, DT, imp) input — what FUSE produces with act.ActorTGLF.lump_ions = true —
# is used as is.
#
# Physics values below are a real STEP case (flat-top, rho = 0.7, from the
# same input.gacode corpus; regenerated for the ukstep_26 linear-CGYRO
# campaign, so gradients differ slightly from the database row). Replace them
# with your own; keep the switches.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

